1. Check if `gcloud` is installed and ask me which Google Cloud PROJECT_ID to use (you can list my projects with `gcloud projects list --limit=10` or check `gcloud config get-value project`).
2. Enable the Gemini Notebook API on that project:
   gcloud services enable notebook.googleapis.com --project="$PROJECT_ID"
3. Authenticate Application Default Credentials (ADC) with a personal Google Account (Google Workspace accounts are not yet supported) that has signed in to https://notebook.google.com at least once, requesting the `notebook` OAuth scope (standard `gcloud auth print-access-token` lacks this scope):
   gcloud auth application-default login --scopes="https://www.googleapis.com/auth/cloud-platform,https://www.googleapis.com/auth/notebook"
4. Mint an access token:
   ACCESS_TOKEN=$(gcloud auth application-default print-access-token)
5. Verify connectivity to `https://notebook.googleapis.com/mcp` using HTTP POST with headers `Authorization: Bearer $ACCESS_TOKEN`, `x-goog-user-project: $PROJECT_ID`, `Content-Type: application/json`, `MCP-Protocol-Version: 2026-07-28`, and `Mcp-Method: tools/list`, sending JSON-RPC `{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 1, "method": "tools/list", "params": 

## Endpoint and authentication

### Other MCP clients

```bash
curl -s -X POST "https://notebook.googleapis.com/mcp" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $ACCESS_TOKEN" \
  -H "x-goog-user-project: $PROJECT_ID" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -H "MCP-Protocol-Version: MCP_PROTOCOL_VERSION" \
  -H "Mcp-Method: tools/list" \
  -d '{
    "jsonrpc": "2.0",
    "id": 1,
    "method": "tools/list",
    "params": {
      "_meta": {
        "io.modelcontextprotocol/protocolVersion": "MCP_PROTOCOL_VERSION"
      }
    }
  }'
```

```bash
CREATE_RESP=$(curl -s -X POST "https://notebook.googleapis.com/mcp" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $ACCESS_TOKEN" \
  -H "x-goog-user-project: $PROJECT_ID" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -H "MCP-Protocol-Version: MCP_PROTOCOL_VERSION" \
  -H "Mcp-Method: tools/call" \
  -H "Mcp-Name: create_notebook" \
  -d '{
    "jsonrpc": "2.0",
    "id": 2,
    "method": "tools/call",
    "params": {
      "name": "create_notebook",
      "arguments": {
        "notebook": {
          "displayName": "MCP Research Notebook"
        }
      },
      "_meta": {
        "io.modelcontextprotocol/protocolVersion": "MCP_PROTOCOL_VERSION"
      }
    }
  }')
